# Copy to .env.local for local development. Never commit the filled-in copy —
# DATABASE_URL contains your database password in plain text.

# ─── Database ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# When set, this overrides data/db-config.json and makes /settings read-only.
# Leave it unset to use the built-in SQLite file (local dev, Coolify, Railway).
#
# Use your provider's POOLED connection string on serverless hosts (Vercel).
# On Neon the pooled host contains "-pooler".
#
# DATABASE_URL="postgresql://user:password@host/dbname?sslmode=require"

# Alternative to DATABASE_URL, if discrete values are easier to manage.
# DB_PROVIDER=postgres        # sqlite | mysql | mariadb | postgres
# DB_HOST=db.example.com
# DB_PORT=5432
# DB_NAME=content_calendar
# DB_USER=cc_user
# DB_PASSWORD=
# DB_SSL=require              # disable | require | verify

# Connections held per server instance. Serverless multiplies this by the
# number of warm instances, so keep it low. Defaults to 2 on Vercel, 5 elsewhere.
# DB_POOL_MAX=2

# ─── First-run protection ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A freshly deployed, publicly reachable instance with no accounts is claimable
# by whoever loads /login first. Set this to require a shared secret during
# admin setup. Only consulted while zero accounts exist; remove it afterwards.
# Generate with: openssl rand -hex 24
# SETUP_TOKEN=
